## Boot

```sh
docker compose up --build
```

Open http://localhost:5173. Choose English or Português (Brasil) in the header
(default catalogs: {{ locales }}). The SPA proxies `/api/health` to FastAPI.
Postgres is included with persistent local storage; this landing does not yet use it.
These containers are for local development. Stop with `docker compose down`.
Set `WEB_PORT` / `API_PORT` if the defaults are occupied.

## Native development (equivalent)

Install Node 24, pnpm 12.9.1, uv, and Docker for Postgres.

```sh
pnpm install
uv sync
docker compose up -d db
pnpm nx run-many -t dev --parallel=2
```

Open http://localhost:5173. API docs: http://localhost:8000/docs.

```sh
pnpm nx run-many -t lint,typecheck,test,build
pnpm nx run api:lock
```

Python dependencies belong to uv; JS dependencies belong to pnpm. Commit the
`uv.lock` and `pnpm-lock.yaml` created at first install. Nx coordinates the
`api` and `web` projects. No hosted services or credentials are needed.
Authentication, payments, deployment and CI are future additions.
Copier records answers for inspection; automatic template updates are not supported yet.
